{"id":"b4b03af7-fc83-4d95-aa02-0a8492c68704","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"50bcb15ffd395431","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/session.ts","baseline":{"blob":"43dcb5bf1a8415781180548bca7b7db3cac6ef43","start":0,"end":63},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","{","createClient","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/util/auth/client","\""]},"context":{"after":"6358c055c8acb4ba"}},"payload":{"text":"Signing in — the shell's side of packages/api (its README.md has the design). Optional: the editor is\nwhole signed out (public repos, samples, everything local), and no account is made until someone signs in. Signing in\ngoes through the API's sign-in page (PAR, C7): GitHub, an emailed code, or a password, two-factor if they've set it\nup. The browser never holds a GitHub token: it holds OUR tokens, DPoP-bound to a key it can't export, and reaches\nGitHub through the API's proxy when the sign-in is GitHub's; signed in by email or a password, it calls GitHub as it\ndoes signed out.\n\nThe client itself is util/auth/client (shared with the admin app): the non-extractable DPoP key in IndexedDB, the\nPKCE round trip (a full page: the shell is cross-origin isolated, which a popup's opener can't survive), refresh, and\n`dpopFetch`, the AuthProvider github.ts and the clone use. This file is the editor's configuration of it (which API,\nwhich pages, which storage names) and the account calls of packages/api/src/account.ts.\n\nShell-side only: the key and the tokens live in the top frame's storage, and no other realm gets a client.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:40:22.005Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:40:22.005Z"}
{"id":"ca55641e-e1c9-4725-b0b5-23eddd39849d","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"52c987126eb007f4","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/session.ts","baseline":{"blob":"c1028f42ae6b59ffff3df8a86d1fa0cd3a10d732","start":2770,"end":2874},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","interface","Me","{","\"","user","\"",":","string",";","\"","githubId","\"",":","number","|","null",";","\"","email","\"",":","{","\"","address","\"",":","string","}","|","null","}"]},"context":{"before":"48a529b3d757bad7","after":"49916876eca25fe0"}},"payload":{"text":"── Your sessions and your account (packages/api/src/account.ts) ────────────────────────────────────────────────","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:40:11.010Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:40:11.010Z"}
{"id":"e3103cac-488f-4bc0-b1ee-68c308527955","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"6358c055c8acb4ba","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/session.ts","baseline":{"blob":"81d52cdf75082847eb6ed689aca3d7460ec73391","start":1240,"end":1298},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","{","isProduction",",","PRODUCTION",",","site","}","from","\"","./address","\""]},"context":{"before":"50bcb15ffd395431","after":"5f8cdaad0a21f0d8"}},"payload":{"text":"The redirect URI is the site's root, a deep link's (`env/<owner>/<repo>`) too: the API knows one page per site, and the\nsign-in's `returnTo` brings us back to the deep link.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:40:20.260Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:40:20.260Z"}
